        <div class="bh-plan__side">
          <ol class="bh-steps">
            <li class="bh-step" data-view="525 360 1000" data-rooms="">
              <p class="ve-label ve-kicker">Arrival to rest</p>
              <h2 class="bh-step__title" id="planTitle">A house opened <em>to a few.</em></h2>
              <p>The Tea Bungalow is not approached as a hotel. It is a private residence opened to a small number of guests: a colonial planter&rsquo;s home built circa 1890 on Galaha Estate, in the misty central highlands. Walk through it, room by room.</p>
            </li>
            <li class="bh-step" data-view="525 470 390" data-rooms="porch morning">
              <figure class="bh-step__photo"><img src="/media/lounge-windows-900.webp" alt="The Morning Room, its tall curtained windows and white-painted benches" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></figure>
              <p class="bh-step__no">01 &middot; Arrival</p>
              <h3 class="bh-step__title">The car porch &amp; <em>Morning Room</em></h3>
              <p>Guests arrive beneath the original car porch and step into the Morning Room, a light-filled reception room where early tea is poured, the day&rsquo;s plans are made and the house begins to breathe.</p>
              <ul class="bh-step__tags"><li>Tea on arrival</li><li>Tall windows</li><li>East light</li></ul>
            </li>
            <li class="bh-step" data-view="395 455 330" data-rooms="salon">
              <figure class="bh-step__photo"><img src="/media/lounge-arches-900.webp" alt="A lamp-lit salon seen through twin arched doorways" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></figure>
              <p class="bh-step__no">02 &middot; Through twin arches</p>
              <h3 class="bh-step__title">The Evening <em>Salon</em></h3>
              <p>An intimate room for conversation, aperitifs and unhurried evenings, named for its late-afternoon light: warm, amber, falling through the original plantation shutters.</p>
              <ul class="bh-step__tags"><li>Plantation shutters</li><li>Aperitif hour</li><li>Candlelit</li></ul>
            </li>
            <li class="bh-step" data-view="480 290 380" data-rooms="table">
              <p class="bh-step__no">03 &middot; The heart of the house</p>
              <h3 class="bh-step__title">The Long <em>Table</em></h3>
              <p>It seats twelve. Estate breakfasts are taken here and slow suppers served by candlelight, and its doors open straight onto the rear verandah and, beyond it, the tea.</p>
              <ul class="bh-step__tags"><li>Seats twelve</li><li>Estate breakfast</li><li>Opens to the verandah</li></ul>
            </li>
            <li class="bh-step" data-view="500 150 600" data-rooms="verandah pavilion">
              <p class="bh-step__no">04 &middot; Outdoors</p>
              <h3 class="bh-step__title">The Long Verandah &amp; <em>Tea Pavilion</em></h3>
              <p>The verandah runs the full rear length of the house: corridor, reading room and mist-watching platform in one. Beyond it, the covered Tea Pavilion hosts live cooking and lantern-lit suppers at the garden&rsquo;s edge.</p>
              <ul class="bh-step__tags"><li>Full-length verandah</li><li>Live cooking</li><li>Lantern dining</li></ul>
            </li>
            <li class="bh-step" data-view="325 270 330" data-rooms="lounge">
              <figure class="bh-step__photo"><img src="/media/lounge-fireplace-900.webp" alt="The Planter's Lounge with its fireplace wall and lamps" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></figure>
              <p class="bh-step__no">05 &middot; The old estate kitchen</p>
              <h3 class="bh-step__title">The Planter&rsquo;s Lounge <em>&amp; Billiards</em></h3>
              <p>Once the estate kitchen, now a room of warm company and slow games. The original stone hearth, lit every evening at six-thirty, anchors it; a billiards table and leather armchairs do the rest.</p>
              <ul class="bh-step__tags"><li>Original hearth</li><li>Lit at 6:30 PM</li><li>Billiards</li></ul>
            </li>
            <li class="bh-step" data-view="540 360 800" data-rooms="galaha camellia verandah-ch pekoe highlands founders founders-v">
              <figure class="bh-step__photo"><img src="/media/chamber-founders-900.webp" alt="The Founder's Suite" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></figure>
              <p class="bh-step__no">06 &middot; Throughout the house</p>
              <h3 class="bh-step__title">Six <em>chambers</em></h3>
              <p>Each individually named and furnished: the Founder&rsquo;s Suite with its own verandah, the Highlands Suite and Pekoe Room as a family wing, the Verandah Chamber opening onto the verandah, and the Camellia and Galaha rooms.</p>
              <a class="ve-link bh-step__link" href="/our-chambers">Look inside every chamber <span aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span></a>
            </li>
            <li class="bh-step" data-view="880 440 330" data-rooms="pool founders-v">
              <figure class="bh-step__photo"><img src="/media/garden-900.webp" alt="The estate garden and tree line" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></figure>
              <p class="bh-step__no">07 &middot; The garden</p>
              <h3 class="bh-step__title">The Private <em>Pool</em></h3>
              <p>Just beyond the Founder&rsquo;s Suite verandah, a small stone-edged pool among tea-border planting and evening jasmine, lantern-lit after dark. Not a resort pool but a garden retreat, best for one or two at a time. A larger estate pool is planned for a later phase.</p>
              <ul class="bh-step__tags"><li>Natural stone</li><li>Teak loungers</li><li>Lantern-lit</li></ul>
            </li>
            <li class="bh-step" data-view="130 525 300" data-rooms="cottage">
              <figure class="bh-step__photo"><img src="/media/chamber-carriage-900.webp" alt="The Carriage House Cottage" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></figure>
              <p class="bh-step__no">08 &middot; A house of its own</p>
              <h3 class="bh-step__title">The Carriage House <em>Cottage</em></h3>
              <p>A former estate outbuilding, now a fully independent two-bedroom residence within the grounds, with its own living room and kitchen, and step-free throughout.</p>
              <ul class="bh-step__tags"><li>Two bedrooms</li><li>Own kitchen</li><li>Step-free</li></ul>
            </li>
          </ol>
          <p class="bh-plan__count" aria-hidden="true"><span class="bh-plan__now">00</span> / 08</p>
